 "description": "Hull nose special armour at ~50 deg (side view): 40 mm high-hardness exterior plate, six steel-rubber NERA packets with gaps, 110 mm inner plate. The glacis above relies on its extreme slope. Estimates vs long rods ~500-620 mm. Reconstruction from public sources (Tankograd, Below The Turret Ring, Zaloga/Wikipedia, forum analyses); real tank armour is secret. Armour amount = public protection estimate / mass efficiency (NERA ~1.3-1.5, Soviet arrays ~1.17). The explosive inside ERA is an empty gap until explosives are added, and the model under-represents NERA breaking long rods - so a full simulation is penetrated more easily than the real armour; the Tank check uses the estimates. 2D slice.",
